    "summary": "The Federal Government of Somalia condemned Houthi attacks on Abha and King Khalid international airports in Saudi Arabia, calling them violations of international law and threats to regional stability.",
    "content": "Mogadishu, October 9, 2026 — The Federal Government of Somalia has strongly condemned attacks on Abha and King Khalid international airports in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, which it attributed to the Houthi group. According to a statement, the attacks resulted in civilian casualties and injuries.\n\nThe government described the attacks as violations of international law and threats to Saudi Arabia's sovereignty and overall regional security. It reaffirmed Somalia's solidarity with Saudi Arabia.\n\nSomalia and Saudi Arabia maintain longstanding ties, with Saudi Arabia hosting a significant Somali diaspora and providing humanitarian and development support. The Houthi movement has been involved in the Yemeni conflict since 2014, and cross-border attacks on Saudi Arabia have occurred previously.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, many of whom reside in Saudi Arabia, such attacks raise concerns about safety and regional stability. The Saudi government has not yet issued a detailed response to the Somali statement.\n\nThis condemnation aligns with Somalia's broader diplomatic stance against terrorism and support for international law.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/09/dowladda-soomaaliya-oo-cambaareysay-weerarrada-lagu-qaaday-garoomada-diyaaradaha-sacuudiga/",
