    "content": "In its latest audience feedback report covering 1-7 October 2026, Radio Ergo documented mixed weather conditions across Somalia. According to callers to the network's independent nationwide platform, the deyr seasonal rains have begun in several areas, including parts of Somaliland, Hirshabelle, Bay region, and certain districts of Jubaland. Some listeners described the rainfall as heavy or continuous.\n\nAt the same time, many other callers reported ongoing drought or very hot and dry conditions. These reports came particularly from central regions, Sanag in the north, a few areas in Bay region earlier in the week, and numerous locations in Gedo region's Dollow district.\n\nThe deyr rains, which typically fall between October and December, are critical for pasture, water sources, and crop production in Somalia. The mixed reports highlight the uneven onset of the season and the continuing impact of prolonged drought in some areas.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, these updates provide valuable insight into conditions affecting family members and communities back home. Many diaspora members rely on such feedback to plan remittances, support livelihoods, and make informed decisions about travel or investments.\n\nThe feedback also underscores the importance of independent, listener-driven reporting in a context where access to reliable information can be limited. Radio Ergo's platform continues to serve as a vital link between local communities and the wider Somali public, including those abroad.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Ergo here: https://radioergo.org/en/2026/10/radio-ergo-audience-feedback-report-1-7-oct-2026/",
